<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see some rain west, sun east.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see some rain west, sun east.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Thursday were forecast to see scattered rain in the west, sun in the east, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see scattered showers with sunny skies in the Peace River Valley and highs of 18 to 24 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see a mix of sun and cloud with highs of 26 to 32 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see sunny and windy conditions with highs of 30 to 32 Celsius.</p>
<p>((--Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
